v class="khcl-meta"><span class="khcl-label" style="background:#5ed29f;color:#fff">New</span><span class="khcl-date">Sep 22, 2026</span></div><div class="khcl-title">ğŸ¥ NEW VIDEO: Sleep and wakefulness</div><div class="khcl-body">Sleep is a temporary state of unconsciousness from which you can be awakened by internal or external stimuli. It plays an important role in daily function, and although its exact purpose is still not </div></div><div class="khcl-item" data-slug="2026-08-04-new-video-reflex-arcs" data-post-id="2502"><div class="khcl-meta"><span class="khcl-label" style="background:#5ed29f;color:#fff">New</span><span class="khcl-date">Sep 15, 2026</span></div><div class="khcl-title">ğŸ¥ NEW VIDEO: Reflex arcs</div><div class="khcl-body">Reflexes are rapid, automatic, involuntary responses to specific stimuli. They help protect the body from injury and support important functions such as posture, muscle tone, heart rate, and respirati</div></div><div class="khcl-item" data-slug="2026-08-04-new-video-olfactory-nerve" data-post-id="2501"><div class="khcl-meta"><span class="khcl-label" style="background:#5ed29f;color:#fff">New</span><span class="khcl-date">Sep 8, 2026</span></div><div class="khcl-title">ğŸ¥ NEW VIDEO: Olfactory nerve</div><div class="khcl-body">The olfactory nerve, also known as cranial nerve I, is responsible for the sense of smell. It detects chemical stimuli called odorants and sends this information to brain regions involved not only in </div></div><div class="khcl-item" data-slug="2026-08-04-new-video-motor-neurons" data-post-id="2500"><div class="khcl-meta"><span class="khcl-label" style="background:#5ed29f;color:#fff">New</span><span class="khcl-date">Sep 1, 2026</span></div><div class="khcl-title">ğŸ¥ NEW VIDEO: Motor neurons</div><div class="khcl-body">Motor neurons carry commands from the central nervous system to effectors such as muscles and glands. In the somatic motor system, they allow skeletal muscles to contract, making voluntary and involun</div></div><div class="khcl-item" data-slug="2026-08-04-new-video-learning-and-memory" data-post-id="2499"><div class="khcl-meta"><span class="khcl-label" style="background:#5ed29f;color:#fff">New</span><span class="khcl-date">Aug 25, 2026</span></div><div class="khcl-title">ğŸ¥ NEW VIDEO: Learning and memory</div><div class="khcl-body">Learning is the acquisition of new information, skills, or behaviors, while memory is the storage and retrieval of that knowledge. These processes are closely linked: learning gives the brain new info</div></div><div class="khcl-item" data-slug="2026-08-04-new-video-cortical-and-brainstem-control-of-motor-functions" data-post-id="2498"><div class="khcl-meta"><span class="khcl-label" style="background:#5ed29f;color:#fff">New</span><span class="khcl-date">Aug 18, 2026</span></div><div class="khcl-title">ğŸ¥ NEW VIDEO: Cortical and brainstem control of motor functions</div><div class="khcl-body">Motor control depends on coordinated activity across the brain, brainstem, spinal cord, and muscles. Even simple movements require the nervous system to plan, execute, and monitor motor activity so th</div></div><div class="khcl-item" data-slug="2026-08-04-new-video-cognition-and-language" data-post-id="2497"><div class="khcl-meta"><span class="khcl-label" style="background:#5ed29f;color:#fff">New</span><span class="khcl-date">Aug 11, 2026</span></div><div class="khcl-title">ğŸ¥ NEW VIDEO: Cognition and language</div><div class="khcl-body">Cognition refers to the brain processes that allow you to perceive, remember, reason, solve problems, and interpret the world around you. Language is one of the most advanced cognitive functions, allo</div></div><div class="khcl-item" data-slug="2026-08-04-new-video-autonomic-nervous-system" data-post-id="2496"><div class="khcl-meta"><span class="khcl-label" style="background:#5ed29f;color:#fff">New</span><span class="khcl-date">Aug 4, 2026</span></div><div class="khcl-title">ğŸ¥ NEW VIDEO: Autonomic nervous system</div><div class="khcl-body">The autonomic nervous system, or ANS, helps regulate essential body functions that happen automatically, such as heart rate, breathing, digestion, pupil size, and other processes that maintain homeost</div></div><div class="khcl-item" data-slug="2026-07-16-new-quiz-summary" data-post-id="2491"><div class="khcl-meta"><span class="khcl-label" style="background:#0099FF;color:#fff">Improvement</span><span class="khcl-date">Jul 16, 2026</span></div><div class="khcl-title">ğŸ‰ New quiz summary</div><div class="khcl-body">We've redesigned the quiz summary you see after every study session - it's now simpler, clearer, and a lot more motivating:Why we changed itThe old summary tried to do too much. Different percentage n</div></div><div class="khcl-item" data-slug="2026-06-17-new-video-mechanoreceptive-somatic-senses" data-post-id="2482"><div class="khcl-meta"><span class="khcl-label" style="background:#5ed29f;color:#fff">New</span><span class="khcl-date">Jun 29, 2026</span></div><div class="khcl-title">ğŸ¥ NEW VIDEO: Mechanoreceptive somatic senses</div><div class="khcl-body">Mechanoreceptive somatic senses allow you to perceive mechanical stimuli acting on the body, such as touch, pressure, vibration, and body position. These sensations depend on specialized sensory recep</div></div><div class="khcl-item" data-slug="2026-06-17-new-video-pain-and-thermal-sensations" data-post-id="2481"><div class="khcl-meta"><span class="khcl-label" style="background:#5ed29f;color:#fff">New</span><span class="khcl-date">Jun 22, 2026</span></div><div class="khcl-title">ğŸ¥ NEW VIDEO: Pain and thermal sensations</div><div class="khcl-body">Pain and thermal sensations help protect the body by detecting potentially harmful stimuli, such as extreme temperatures, sharp pressure, or tissue damage. These sensations rely on specialized recepto</div></div><div class="khcl-item" data-slug="2026-06-16-new-video-glial-cells" data-post-id="2480"><div class="khcl-meta"><span class="khcl-label" style="background:#5ed29f;color:#fff">New</span><span class="khcl-date">Jun 16, 2026</span></div><div class="khcl-title">ğŸ¥ NEW VIDEO: Glial cells</div><div class="khcl-body">Glial cells, also known as neuroglia, are essential support cells of the nervous system. While neurons are responsible for transmitting nerve impulses, glial cells help maintain the right environment </div></div><div class="khcl-item" data-slug="2026-05-21-quizzes-just-got-a-major-upgrade" data-post-id="2472"><div class="khcl-meta"><span class="khcl-label" style="background:#0099FF;color:#fff">Improvement</span><span class="khcl-date">May 21, 2026</span></div><div class="khcl-title">ğŸ‰ Quizzes just got a major upgrade</div><div class="khcl-body">You can now choose which content to include in your study sessions. Plus a simpler layout and a faster way to start.Pick exactly what you want to learnGo to any study session inside a study unit and c</div></div></div></div><div class="khcl-view khcl-view-detail"><div class="khcl-empty">Loading...</div></div></div></div>

